  texture_mask: {fileID: 0}
  title: Overpressure
  text: 'The power of a round is determined by the mass and the velocity of its bullet.
    If you want your shots to hit with more force, you either need to upgrade to
    a bigger caliber, or switch to +P loads. Overpressure, or +P rounds, are rounds
    loaded with a higher concentration of gunpowder, which gives the fired bullet
    increased stopping power, basically guaranteeing that whatever you shoot down,
    will stay down -- at least long enough for you to safely neutralize your target.


    Advantages
    rarely come without disadvantages however, and +P rounds are no exception. If
    you''re a novice shooter, the brighter flash and increased recoil might take
    you by surprise and cause you to flinch -- or the added stress to the firearm''s
    mechanics might prevent the gun from cycling properly, or the casing might expand
    too much and get stuck the chamber, making it harder to extract. '
  end_padding_seconds: 0
